		{"id":"62c3c910736339e5","type":"text","text":"# **Homework** \n### **Exercises 31-32**. Countries & Cultures: Singapore, **exercises 33-35.**","x":-325,"y":32,"width":650,"height":138,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"a40e49dec9d4422f","type":"text","text":"\n## **10:50** -\tReading\n## **11:10** - Countries and Cultures Singapore\n## **11:35** - Homework \n","x":-324,"y":-163,"width":649,"height":156,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"bc5d6b4dc39788d2","type":"text","text":"# **Today's Class: Reviewing the Test**","x":-301,"y":-264,"width":602,"height":68,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"6d7412f2e5f38f1d","type":"text","text":"## Why do people in Singapore speak English, and why can Singaporean English sound different?","x":672,"y":-261,"width":502,"height":130},
		{"id":"b6269c925cdf428e","type":"file","file":"Documenten/Bijlages/90s_kids_share.mp4","x":723,"y":32,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"2745f61ee6aaecca","type":"text","text":"**Geography and history:** Singapore is a country in Southeast Asia. Britain established a trading post there in **1819**, and Singapore was subsequently ruled by Britain. English became associated with trade, administration and some schools.","x":1309,"y":-226,"width":446,"height":167},
		{"id":"b840b7750f1fccf3","type":"text","text":"**Why English?** English connects people whose home languages differ. It is also useful in schooling, government, international business and communication beyond Singapore. The choice has roots in colonial history, but post-independence policy developed its everyday role.","x":1248,"y":258,"width":600,"height":136},
		{"id":"cf7e9f226eb548ac","type":"text","text":"![[18 November-1794993721347.webp]]","x":1276,"y":-596,"width":512,"height":335},
		{"id":"c269424f2c2f2739","type":"text","text":"**Singapore is not part of Malaysia** because it separated on **August 9, 1965**, becoming an independent nation after less than two years in the Malaysian federation. It also has a predominantly ethnic Chinese population rather than a Malay majority.","x":1848,"y":-226,"width":580,"height":129},
		{"id":"4c34e6635b4fbd06","type":"text","text":"**Investing in Human Capital:** Lacking natural resources, the nation poured resources into top-tier education, technical schools, and an English-speaking, highly skilled workforce.","x":1883,"y":-59,"width":545,"height":120},
		{"id":"2cdf68edd070f63f","type":"text","text":"**Singapore English:** Standard English in formal settings; informal \n**Singlish** in many everyday situations.  \n**Listen respectfully:** differences are not automatically mistakes.","x":1947,"y":109,"width":418,"height":246},
		{"id":"60bd9a12286b9af4","type":"text","text":"**Four official languages:** **English, Malay, Mandarin Chinese and Tamil**. **Malay is the national language**, while English is the main common **working language**.","x":1289,"y":32,"width":488,"height":116}
	],
